<title>HUNGARY: Konzum swings to loss in Jan-Sept.</title>
<headline>Konzum swings to loss in Jan-Sept.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period ending on September 30.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>				    '96 Jan-Sept	    '95 Jan-Sept</p>
<p>    Group operating result	75.9 loss   vs     30.2 profit</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax result	 141.7 loss   vs	3.6 profit</p>
<p>    Group net sales		911.5	  vs  1,953.8</p>
<p>     Group foreign sales	 341.9	  vs    355.8</p>
<p>     Group domestic sales	569.5	  vs  1,598.0</p>
<p>    Group extraordinary result  14.9 loss   vs     11.7 loss</p>
<p>    Material expenditures	635.8	  vs  1,530.0 @</p>
<p>    Personal expenditures	239.5	  vs    296.8</p>
<p>    Depreciation		    48.7	  vs     50.1</p>
<p>    Other costs		     90.0	  vs    107.6</p>
<p>    Other expenditures	    33.3	  vs     36.5</p>
<p>Result of financial</p>
<p>	   operations		 50.9 loss   vs     14.9 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - Konzum Rt is an industrial and retail holding compnay. The largest single shareholder of Konzum is Osterreichische Kontrollbank, which holds 24.3 percent of the shares.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom, 36 1 (327 4040</p>
</text>
